      "publication_year": 2021,
      "publication_date": "2021-01-01",
      "abstract": "The year 2021 marks the 150th anniversary of Rosa Luxemburg\u2019s birth. Even though she met a violent death in the course of the 1918/19 revolution and much has subsequently been done to diminish her memory, her works remain an inspiration to this day for all those who seek to create a new, better, and more just world. This volume brings together works by German-speaking and international scholars who address Luxembourg\u2019s aftermath from different perspectives and with different questions. In their entirety, they underscore the important significance that Luxemburg\u2019s thoughts still have today.",
